"""29 October 2026 : ZenRay Lines TRI PATCH, a component with THREE corners (a pointed window, a sail) made of three quad grids
around one centre pole of valence 3 (the midpoint pattern of Takayama, Panozzo, Sorkine-Hornung 2014) : no quad is crushed at the
point, every quad stays square, the three grids share their spokes (welded).
EN: counts : sides n0, n1, n2 split as p, q, s with n0 = p + s, n1 = q + p, n2 = s + q (n0 + n1 + n2 even) ; spokes r0 = q, r1 = s,
r2 = p. Each grid : Tutte then harmonic interior in the view plane, lifted on the fair field of the component (ZrrPatch.Field).
The judge (ZrrCheck) runs on every grid closed as a panel ; at an outline corner sharper than 30 degrees the corner quad is held to
0.9 sin(angle) (no quad can be squarer than the corner it sits in), every other quad to 0.5.
python ZrlTri.py <component>        FR : un component à trois coins, trois grilles de quads autour d'un pôle de valence 3."""
import json, os, sys
import numpy as np
from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix
from scipy.sparse.linalg import spsolve
from PIL import Image, ImageDraw, ImageFont
